        <mxCell id="c155" value="&lt;i&gt;Selected: D3, which holds =B24, the break-even revenue with the added items (19,959,700). Outlined: the cell for 45% and 9,000,000, the nearest to the model&#x27;s own ratio (45.0%) and fixed costs (8,979,457); it reads 20,000,000. The table is built with B9 as the row input cell and B23 as the column input cell, and every grid cell is the one array formula {=TABLE(B9,B23)}. Columns A to C hold the model and are not shown.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="346" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
